# Mandatory testing trio (LOCKED)

**User order (lifetime):** Har project / har slice ke baad ye **3 tests lazmi**. Skip **NA**.  
**Scope:** Master Admin (`mieraf-ksa.com/master`) + **har store** dashboard + storefront (flowers, coffee, bleco, future tenants) — sab mein.

## 1) Gitleaks — secrets (pehle)
- Scan repo / changed paths for leaked keys, tokens, passwords, `.env` commits.
- Fail → **fix pehle**, deploy mat socho.
- Never commit secrets; never print tokens in toasts/logs/UI.

## 2) Autocannon — load (API / critical routes)
- Hit live (or staging) **health + key APIs** per affected host/`store_id`.
- Master + each touched store: `/api/health`, catalog/products, auth gate as relevant.
- Report: RPS, latency p50/p99, error %. Spike errors → fix before “done”.
- Soft load only unless user asks heavy stress (do not DDoS production).

## 3) Lighthouse — page quality (UI surfaces)
- Run on touched public/admin URLs: storefront home, key shop pages, `/admin`, `/master` when Master changed.
- Check Performance + Accessibility + Best Practices + SEO (public pages).
- No fake score decoration — real report only. Regressions → fix or call out clearly.

## When to run
- After meaningful UI, API, auth, SEO, or deploy-path changes.
- Before claiming **Ho gaya** on Master or any store.
- Multi-store change → sample **each affected store**, not only one demo tenant.

## Banned
- “Code looks fine” without trio (when surface was touched)
- Testing only flowers and skipping other stores / Master
- Inventing Lighthouse scores or Autocannon numbers
- Running destructive/full-blast load that takes down Hostinger

## Status (Roman Urdu)
End with **Ho gaya** / **Baqi** + short trio result (Gitleaks clean? Autocannon OK? Lighthouse notes?).
